# Realms — GDD v0.1

> **Status: designed with the owner on 2026-11-28.** Built so far (§16): the boss's ultimate
> (v0.12.19), the realm core (v0.12.20), and the Black Prison as the first sub-realm with the
> arena's preloaded spaces, the camera per space and the window (v0.12.21). The engine
> contract is `Docs/Tech/T50-REALMS.md`. Not built yet: the tsunami (still the beach's one-shot
> hazard), lenses, the realm sound, items and other weathers.

## 1. The idea

Fableland is worlds torn from different storybooks. A **realm** makes that literal inside a
fight: a character, a boss, an item or a map's weather opens a **sub-realm** — another world's
ground under a patch of the battlefield — and whoever is caught is *in that world* until they
get out. The owner calls this a core concept of the game: many protagonists, bosses, items
and weathers will use it, so it is one system with data, not a trick per skill.

## 2. Words

| Word | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Main realm** | The battlefield: the map the fight was dealt. |
| **Sub-realm** | Another world a body can be inside. Each open one is an **instance**, named (`prison#2`), made from a **definition** (the horror patch). |
| **Definition** | What a sub-realm is: a full interactive **map** (e.g. a VOID boss's void space) or a **patch** (the Black Prison's horror world). |
| **Region** | Where the sub-realm sits in the main realm: a circle, or a moving shape (a wave). |
| **Anchors** | A point in the main realm and its partner in the sub-realm. |
| **Ratio** | Sub-realm metres per main-realm metre. 2 = everything inside is twice as far apart. |
| **Exit border** | The line in the sub-realm that leads back out: the region's edge, times the ratio. |
| **Window** | What someone in the main realm sees where a region is: the sub-realm inside it. |
| **Lens** | A colour rule on the window. The outside view may lie about the inside. |

## 3. Who can open one

| Source | Example | Status |
|---|---|---|
| A protagonist's skill | PumpKing's Black Prison (Q) | **built v0.12.21**, §12 |
| A boss's skill | BOSS PumpKing's Black Prison; a VOID boss dragging you into the void space | §13; the void space TBD #95 |
| An item | — (none yet) | TBD |
| A map's **weather** — an environment hazard the map carries | the beach's tsunami drags you into the Loong's Palace | §14 |

## 4. The projection — anchors and ratio (the owner's rule)

Every instance carries a tuple **(main anchor, sub anchor, instance name, ratio)**. A position
in one realm has exactly one partner in the other:

- into the sub-realm: `sub = subAnchor + ratio × (main − mainAnchor)`
- back out: `main = mainAnchor + (sub − subAnchor) ÷ ratio`

Everything follows from it:
- **No slows needed.** At ratio 2 a body walks at its normal speed inside, but the exit
  border is twice as far: leaving takes twice as long, measured in the main realm.
- **Small outside, vast inside.** A 1 m circle at ratio 20 is a 20 m world, hard to escape.
- **Wormholes.** The main anchor may **move** while the realm stands. You come out relative to
  where it is *now*, somewhere other than where you went in (§14, the tsunami).
- The ratio is the same across and up (circles stay circles, a jump stays a jump).

## 5. Going in

- **Who:** anyone in scope — every protagonist, foe and boss of **either side**, the caster
  included. A ranged caster who opens it under his own feet chose to (the owner). Never pulled
  in: projectiles, ground, platforms, hazards, mission objectives, pickups, wonder cores, props.
- **When:** as the realm opens, and — if its definition says so — whenever someone walks into
  the region while it stands.
- **Where you land:** your projected position, nudged a little inside the exit border so one
  step back doesn't throw you out. Landing in mid-air: you fall. Landing inside ground: you are
  moved to the nearest open spot.
- **Your momentum is kept** as it was (not multiplied by the ratio).

## 6. Inside

- You stand on the sub-realm's ground and see **only the sub-realm**. **You cannot see the
  border:** a definition's ground and art go on past its exit border, so nothing marks the way
  out.
- You can hit and be hit only by bodies, projectiles and hazards **of the same realm** (§8).
- The definition's own rules apply (the prison: silence on the caster's enemies; §12) and its
  own creatures and hazards (the prison's pumpkins). A realm may carry its world's laws
  (gravity, swimming — `MapGDD.md` §2.3).
- Time runs at the same rate (a time ratio is TBD #91).

## 7. Coming out

Three ways:
1. **Cross the exit border** (from inside). You land at your projected main position, nudged a
   little outside the region.
2. **The realm closes.** Everyone inside lands at their projected main positions.
3. **Your own time is up** — for realms that carry you for a while (the tsunami, §14).

Landing inside ground moves you to the nearest open spot; past the map's edge, to the edge.
After coming out you cannot be pulled back into the same instance for **0.5 s**, so standing
on the edge does not bounce you in and out.

## 8. Across the border: nothing, in the first version

The owner's question (2026-11-28): if only PumpKing could attack from outside, the prisoners
could not fight back; if everything crosses, bugs. **Decided for v1: nothing crosses in
either direction.** A shot fired at the region from outside flies through it; a shot inside
stays inside; hits, area blasts, auras and target lists see only their own realm.
- **It is fair:** a caster who stays outside cannot touch the prisoners either, and they
  cannot touch him. His way in is the recast, which takes him inside, where they can hit back.
- **It is safe:** a projectile never has to be projected, sped up or slowed at a border, and
  never orphaned when a realm closes with it inside.
- **Later, by design:** a specific skill may be made a *portal* (say, a bomb that may be
  thrown into a realm), one at a time with its own check — TBD #92.

## 9. Seeing and hearing

- **From inside:** only the sub-realm (§6).
- **From outside:** the region is a **window**. The sub-realm is drawn into it shrunk by the
  ratio, prisoners at their projected spots, so a caster can watch and time his recast.
- **The lens:** a window may show the inside through a colour rule — a palette swap. One set
  of sprites serves both views. *The owner's example:* from outside the sub-realm looks
  beautiful, cloud and fog under a soft sky; you jump in and it is hell, and the cloud and fog
  are burning. The same trick gives a map its night and morning from one sheet (TBD #90).
- **Sound inside:** the sub-realm's own sound, plus the main scene's sound **twisted, hollow
  and muffled** — dreamcore, the decayed-ballroom feel of The Caretaker's records.
- **Sound outside:** the sub-realm's sound muffled the same way (proposed; TBD #94).

## 10. Missions

Objectives stay in the main realm, and **the mission clock keeps running** while you are away.
A protect target can be lost while its guard is in a sub-realm.

## 11. Limits in the first version

- **No nesting:** a body in a sub-realm is never pulled into another, and a skill that opens a
  realm cannot be used inside one (it is refused with the usual "can't use that" toast).
  Projections would chain neatly, so this can open later (TBD #93).
- **Two instances never share a space:** two Black Prisons are two horror worlds.
- **Silence and items:** a silenced body uses no skill and no item (`ITEMS.gdd` §3.3).

## 12. The Black Prison as a sub-realm — *built v0.12.21*

| | Number |
|---|---|
| Warning | 1 s, on the battlefield, as now |
| Region | a circle, **8 m** radius, centred where he aims (≤ 8 m from him) |
| Sub-realm | a **patch** of PumpKing's horror world, the Dark Wood |
| Ratio | **2** — the exit border is **16 m** from the patch's centre; the patch goes on well past it (about 24 m) |
| Pulled in | everyone in the circle as it forms, him included; and anyone who walks in while it stands |
| Inside | **silence on the caster's enemies only** (skills and items). **No** slow, **no** jump limit, **no** sight limit |
| Pumpkins | every 0.5 s (8 in all), one grows at a **random** spot in the patch and is **shot in a random direction**: 10–25 damage by size, no shove; they hit only the caster's enemies and never leave the patch |
| Recast | Q again, free, once, after it forms: his mouth opens at the patch's centre (0.4 s), he blinks there (entering if he was outside) and his head's biggest blast goes off: 3 m, 100 × his damage multiplier, no shove |
| Ends | 4 s after forming; everyone inside comes out at their projected positions |
| From outside | a window onto the horror world, half size, through the Dark Wood's lens (TBD #90) |

Gone since v0.12.21: the move and jump scales, the 3 m sight cap, the dark veil, pumpkins
grown at the heart and thrown outward, pumpkins hitting outside. The caster may recast from
inside or outside. Pumpkin numbers wait for play tests; for now they are random.

**As built (v0.12.21):**
- The patch is a small map document, `Maps/Realms/kh_black_prison.json` (30 × 18 cells: a
  floor, seven branches to stand on, the Dark Wood's far layers, the moon), made by
  `Tools/realm_maps/build_realm_patches.py`. Its spawn marker is the sub anchor. It lives under
  `Maps/Realms/`, so it is never dealt as a fight.
- Since the cast range and the radius are both 8 m, **he is always in his own circle when he
  casts it**: the farthest he can open it still touches his hit circle. He is pulled in unless
  he steps out during the 1 s warning (from the far edge, under a metre's walk). Once inside he
  can walk out over the 16 m border, and recast to blink back in.
- A crab under the mouth takes the recast's blast from above, which its Soft Shell doubles
  (200). The mouth sits at the anchor, a body's height over the floor.
- From outside, the window shows the patch at half size, clipped to the circle, under the
  prison's black bristling rim: its ground, trees, branches and everyone caught. It does not show
  the patch's far scenery yet (the moon, the far wood; T50 §6), and there is no lens yet: it
  shows the inside as it is. Inside, the camera is held to the patch's art, which covers the whole
  16 m circle and more, so a prisoner never sees the border or the world's end.

## 13. BOSS PumpKing casts his ultimate — *built v0.12.19*

- **A boss's ring:** 1500 to fill, **+10 per second** while the fight runs, **+5 per point of
  damage** he deals or takes. *(Players are unchanged: +1 per damage dealt, +2 per damage
  taken, nothing over time, kept between fights — `NODES.gdd` §3.3.)*
- **When full, he aims 5 m ahead of the player along their moving direction**, so the player
  walks into the centre during the 1 s warning. A player standing still: at the player. In the
  air: at the player's height. Beyond his 8 m cast range: he closes in first.
- **He recasts the moment the prison forms** (blink, the 100-damage blast).

## 14. Weather: the tsunami

Today the beach has a one-shot tsunami: a wave 32 m wide and 16 m tall that crosses the arena
right to left at 15 m/s, costing a third of max HP, a shove and 1 s of no control
(`Scripts/Hazard/TsunamiHazard.cs`). As a realm source:
- the wave is a **moving region**, its main anchor travelling with it;
- whoever it sweeps is pulled into the **Loong's Palace** — the Palace of LOOING's undersea
  world, where everyone swims;
- each rider stays a few seconds (their own timer), then comes out **where the wave is now**,
  further along its path.

Open (TBD #88): the ride time, whether it still hurts or shoves, its direction (the owner
said left to right; today it runs right to left), the ratio, and the Palace's patch.

## 15. No hitch when a realm opens (the owner's rule)

When a map loads, the fight already knows every realm it might need: the battle party's
skills, the boss's, every item the team holds or owns as a Possession, and the map's weather.
Each of those worlds is built **once, before the countdown ends**, switched off. Opening a
realm only switches it on and moves bodies. A full map costs about what the arena does, a
patch far less; T50 §8 sets the budget.

## 16. Build order

1. ~~**BOSS PumpKing casts his ult** with the boss ring (§13).~~ **Built v0.12.19**; the boss
   check's `ProbeBossUlt` proves it (on today's prison — it moves onto the realm in step 3).
2. ~~**The realm core** (T50).~~ **Built:** the core in v0.12.20 (membership by position, the
   filter, going in and coming out — nudges, open spots, the map's edge, the grace, rides —
   no nesting; `RealmCheck` proves them); in v0.12.21 the arena building spaces from map
   documents before the fight (`ArenaRealmSpaces`), the camera and far layers per space and
   the window (`RealmView`, `RealmWindow`).
3. ~~**The Black Prison moves onto it** (§12).~~ **Built v0.12.21:** the horror patch, random
   pumpkins, silence, the window. The boss check's prison probes were rewritten for it.
4. **The tsunami** as the first weather realm (§14), on the beach — VK is the art pilot's
   reference world too.
5. Lenses, the dreamcore sound, then items and other weathers, one at a time.

## 17. Decisions log

- **(2026-11-28) The owner's design.** Sub-realms opened by skills, bosses, items and weather;
  every possible world preloaded with the map; a body in a realm is on another layer.
  Projection by **(main anchor, sub anchor, name, ratio)**; sizes may differ; anchors may move
  (wormholes). Out by crossing the border (which only the main realm shows) or when it closes.
  The ratio replaces the slow; the prison is ratio 2, a 16 m border. Anyone in scope is pulled
  in, the caster included. Only protagonists and foes cross between realms. Objectives stay
  outside and the clock runs. Pumpkins random for now. A realm is a map or a patch. Weather
  example: the tsunami into the Loong's Palace. In the prison: no jump limit, **only silence**.
  The window, with lenses (palette rules) later. Sound: the main scene twisted, hollow and
  muffled, plus the realm's own. Boss ring 1500, +10/s, +5 per damage; players unchanged.
- **(2026-11-28) Proposed by me and accepted ("all other designs follow your suggestions"):**
  a nudge inside on entry and outside on exit, a 0.5 s re-entry grace, the nearest open spot
  for a landing in ground, clamping to the map, patches larger than their exit border,
  objectives never pulled in, the per-body timer as a third way out, no nesting at first,
  momentum kept, one space per instance, silence only on the caster's enemies (he can always
  recast), the boss's aim cases (standing, airborne, out of range).
- **(2026-11-28) Asked of me by the owner — "allow projectiles or not?":** not in v1, in either
  direction (§8). Symmetric, so fair; and the main source of border bugs never exists.
- **(v0.12.21) Found while building the prison:** the cast range and the radius are both 8 m, so
  the caster is always inside his own circle when he casts it, and is pulled in unless he steps
  out during the warning. Kept as the owner's rule ("anyone in scope"); flagged to the owner in
  case he wants to open it from outside and watch (a cast range longer than the radius would
  allow it).
- **(v0.12.21) A foe drops a player who goes into another realm at once,** not after the three
  more looks a foe gives a player who slips out of its sight (FOES §6), and a blow does not
  turn it on a player in another realm.
